[x] Review and commit Decision 55 (VEVENT-only calendar sync) =commit-d55 $Drafted 2026-10-07 in docs/DECISIONS.md, uncommitted; D51's calendar bullet carries an 'Amended by Decision 55' note. Choices made in the draft for the human to confirm: linked VTODO Plans convert to VEVENT for one release, unlinked VTODOs are never adopted (doctor reports them); clearhead export plans keeps one-way VTODO export; name and description merge both ways as an experiment (Left open names how to judge it); the block stays bidirectional. Implementation follows Decision 54's order: specification release first (ics_schedule_spec, process, configuration, workspace, ontology VTODO mapping), then Core. Core note: stage_prepared_plan_token stamps title and description merge bases only for VTODO; under VEVENT-only with name merging that block becomes unconditional.$ !2 +calendar ^2026-10-07T21:57 %2026-10-12T02:39 #01a119df-6999-728a-89e7-b51a201d9eee
[x] Cross-workspace queries return each row twice =query-duplicate-rows $Found 2026-10-13: cross-workspace queries return each row twice. Cause (2026-10-13 later, assistant): the query evaluator sets oxigraph default-graph-as-union (clearhead-cli src/query/sparql/mod.rs execute), and oxigraph unions graphs as a bag, not a set. Shared nodes such as the +human context (deterministic urn:uuid:c50941c3...) carry their rdfs:label triple in every workspace graph that uses them, so one pattern matches once per graph. Repro: a workspace with additional_workspaces \\\\\\\[srr, personal-os] returns 2 rows per +human action; \\\\\\\[srr] alone or \\\\\\\[srr, platform] returns 1. SPARQL defines the default graph as an RDF graph, a set. Proposed fix: store_from also inserts every quad into the default graph (set insert dedupes) and execute stops forcing union; GRAPH ?g queries are unchanged. Regression test: two workspaces sharing a context, for-human returns each action once. Spec: specifications 168d32f (ontology.md, Union Default Graph) now says the union is a set and the default implementation copies every quad into the default graph. Done when: store_from (or the one place the evaluator builds its store) inserts each quad also into the default graph; execute no longer calls set_default_graph_as_union; a Tests: commit first adds a CLI-level test with two workspaces whose actions share a context (e.g. +human) and asserts query named for-human returns each action once, and that a GRAPH ?g query still names each source workspace. Update the module doc comment that describes the union-default-graph convention. DONE 2026-10-13: clearhead-core ebe7336 (Tests:) adds the CLI regression and implements the decided fix. The test uses two workspace identities sharing +human and a saved for-human query without DISTINCT; before the fix it returned Alpha, Alpha, Beta, Beta, afterwards Alpha, Beta. GRAPH ?g still returns each action with its source workspace graph. store_from inserts each published quad unchanged and its triple into the default graph, letting set insertion deduplicate shared nodes; execute no longer forces evaluator union. Module and store documentation describe the materialized set union. Test and implementation share the first Tests: commit so the required gate stays green without weakening the regression. No new dependencies. Full foreground sh scripts/gate.sh passed.$ !3 ^2026-10-13T06:24 %2026-10-13T07:00 #01a133ee-f70a-72b1-8cb1-6b45f923fa95
