[x] Decide where Habits' template bindings live =template-binding-home $From the 2026-10-07 session. Proposal: an X-CLEARHEAD-TEMPLATE:<name> property on the Plan's VEVENT instead of the template: directive in DESCRIPTION. It moves with the .ics (a sidecar binding orphans when a Plan changes collection), is readable plaintext, is hidden from phone UIs so they cannot mangle it, and lets Decision 55 drop its directive guard. Rule behind it: time belongs to the calendar, structure to ClearHead; ownership is not storage. Usability: create from the template (plan add --template <name> --rrule ..., title from the template) and, for phone-created plans, doctor or the LSP proposes a binding when the title matches a template name; never bind automatically. Rejected: the charter sidecar keyed by Plan UID (orphans on move, needs UUIDs or the CLI to write); template frontmatter naming its plans (wrong dependency direction, templates are reused).$ !3 +calendar ^2026-10-07T21:57 %2026-10-16T06:04 <x-prop-survival #01a119df-69bc-7628-a336-d5b908442098
