[x] Cascade cancel overwrites completed children =cancel-keeps-completed $Authorized by Darrion 2026-10-31. Fix cascade cancellation preserving factual closed-child history; no specification change. Reproduced 2026-10-31 with CLI 0.3.2: in a temporary .clearhead/charters/next.actions, an open parent containing a completed child dated 2026-10-01T10:00, a cancelled child dated 2026-10-02T10:00 and an open child; cancel action parent --file <path> succeeds but archives all four as cancelled with today timestamp. Expected: parent and open descendants cancel, completed and already-cancelled descendants retain state and original completed_at (including absent timestamps), and all descendants move together with existing internal parent links. Cause: clearhead-core/crates/clearhead-core/src/domain/mod.rs close_subtree unconditionally assigns state and completed_at to every subtree member. Shared callers: workspace/archive_actions.rs close_action_subtree path and workspace/transaction.rs close_in_file. Tests FIRST: add a focused mixed-state regression exercising close_subtree and demonstrate failure before implementation; include nested open descendants under terminal nodes, unrelated actions unchanged, source immutability, retained intra-tree links and detached root. Add native/CLI archive regression for ordinary cancel and transaction cancel-action with exact original terminal timestamps, no dropped or duplicated nodes and active subtree removal. Then fix the shared cancellation mechanism, not adapter workarounds. Keep complete/reopen behavior outside this cancellation-only scope unchanged; if broader lifecycle semantics need deciding, stop and ask. Update the generated invariant closing_a_generated_subtree_is_local_and_complete in crates/clearhead-core/tests/generated_invariants.rs to assert the corrected cancellation contract, preserving its other coverage and completion assertions. Update stale close_subtree documentation without changing specification. Follow docs/overnight-runbook.md: full Core gate, doctor before/after, commit Core changes then platform pin and action outcome; no push in sandbox. Acceptance: mixed-state cancellation preserves closed history through both APIs, open descendants cancel normally, gates green, separate-vendor review covers Core and platform. Workflow launch deferred: shared review-cycle hard-codes github-copilot provider and cannot currently route work/fix to ChatGPT as required by pace; see workflow-chatgpt-routing action. Original personal-os workaround: cancel open leaves individually and leave parent open. Implemented in Core 8b87a13: shared close_subtree preserves completed/cancelled state and exact original completed_at (including absent values) during cancellation, still traverses terminal nodes to cancel open descendants, moves the entire subtree with internal links and detaches its root. Added focused domain and ordinary/transaction CLI archive regressions; demonstrated all three failing on the original history overwrite before implementation. Corrected plaintext fixture to depth-first order during validation. Updated generated cancellation invariant with completion assertions retained and refreshed lifecycle helper documentation; no specification or complete/reopen behavior changes. Full Core gate green; doctor before/after unchanged at 13 warnings and zero violations. Platform pin updated with this outcome. Review 20261031-223325/6 then found that with this fix, transact cancel-action on a terminal target still in the active file would archive it unchanged and report Cancelled, so Core d03bcb1 (tests) and b9e93fd add a guard: it now returns AlreadyClosed, as ordinary cancel already did. This tightens the transaction API; no caller outside Core in any repository. Platform pin moved in dc21082. Landed 2026-10-31 as Core 0a2e41f and platform 4aaff00, run cancel-keeps-completed-20261031-2233, past Claude review 20261031-223325/8 by override: its one should-fix was this record, corrected here 